<title>USA: Mercantile completes acquisitions.</title>
<headline>Mercantile completes acquisitions.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercantile Bankshares Corp said on Tuesday it completed its acquisitions of Home Bank and Farmers Bank for stock.</p>
<p>Home Bank, based in Newark, Md., had assets of $46 million. Its shareholders received a total of up to 712,826 Mercantile common shares, Mercantile said in a news release.</p>
<p>Farmers Bank, based in Mardela Springs, Md., had assets of $28 million. Its shareholders received up a total of up to 172,553 Mercantile shares.</p>
<p>Both acquired banks will be merged into Peninsula Bank, a Mercantile affiliate.</p>
<p>Mercantile has assets of $6.7 billion. Its shares were up 7/8 to 27-1/2 in afternoon Nasdaq trading.</p>
</text>
